n### \ud83d\udfe1 Changes recommended\n\nCoroutine metadata incorrectly attributes Flow support to the newly default-off annotations selector.\n\n<details open>\n<summary><strong>1 open finding</strong></summary>\n\n- <picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/low-v2-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/low-v2-light.svg\"><img src=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/low-v2-light.png\" alt=\"Low severity\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" align=\"texttop\"></picture> [Clarify selector scope versus Flow support in module metadata](#discussion_r4214348398) \u00b7 New\n</details>\n\n\ud83e\udde0 **Review effort:** Balanced\n\n---\n\nGive feedback about Copilot approvals in [this survey](https://survey.alchemer.com/s3/9011660/CCR-Public-Preview-Autoapprove-feedback-survey) to enter a drawing for a $150 gift card.","comment_id":null,"key":"review:5451069420","kind":"body","line":null,"path":null,"review_id":5451069420},{"body":"[General] The `kotlinx-coroutines-annotations` module only matches suspend methods; Flow-returning methods are handled by the generic annotation instrumentation, while this project's Flow module supplies async completion and remains enabled separately. As written, this metadata incorrectly implies that the new default-off selector controls Flow support. Separate the two behaviors in the description.","comment_commit_id":"c8ea549c30ba872fdced76558a347a8ed10edf0f","comment_id":4214348398,"key":"inline:4214348398","kind":"inline","line":4,"original_commit_id":"c8ea549c30ba872fdced76558a347a8ed10edf0f","original_line":4,"path":"instrumentation/kotlinx-coroutines/kotlinx-coroutines-1.0/metadata.yaml","review_commit_id":"c8ea549c30ba872fdced76558a347a8ed10edf0f","review_id":5451069420,"review_submitted_at":"2026-10-08T03:42:56Z",